BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20260429-cultural-rounds@psychosocial-research-axis
DTSTAMP:20260525T181000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T163000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Cultural Psychiatry Day 2026
LOCATION:Online
DESCRIPTION:Keynote: Resistance to explicit and implicit institutional and governmental erosion of EDI and cultural psychiatry: From daily clinical practice to advocacy coalitions.\nSpeaker: Cecile Rousseau, MD.\nPanels: Lived experiences of EDI, cultural perspectives, and ethnospecific services in education and training.\nClinician Perspectives: Donna Alexander, Lisa Andermann, Alan Fung, Peter Braunnerger.\nResident Perspectives: Fernanda Perez Gay-Juarez, Shuyi Zhai, Johanne Mathieu, Tori Anderson, David Dai, Dina-Liza Ikene.\nResident Presentation: Dawn Veinot (Supervisor: Sarosh Khalid-Khan).\nChair: Laurence J. Kirmayer, MD.\nZoom link will be sent closer to the event.
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/cultural-psychiatry-day-2026-tickets-1986104917272
END:VEVENT

